<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador posts $93 mln trade surplus in March.</title>
<headline>Ecuador posts $93 mln trade surplus in March.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador posted a $93 million trade surplus in March, down from $111 million surplus in the same month last year, the Central Bank said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $423 million, up from $419 million in March 1996. Imports grew to $330 million from $308 million.</p>
<p>In the first three months of 1997, there was a $1.23 billion surplus versus a $1.12 billion surplus in the same period 1996.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
